Reading: the touch on BOTH venues' moneylines sits at the minimum tick —
the quoted spread is a censored bound, not an equilibrium choice. Fee-era
'spread unchanged' is therefore about the bound; depth and volume are the
free margins (volume moved -41%; depth capture now accumulating). In the
tails, Kalshi's uniform cent is a 10-20% relative floor where Polymarket's
0.001 regime floors at 1-2% — tick design, not trader behavior, sets the
price of tail liquidity.

